{"tool_name":"scenery","contents":["neubias","oeb","bioschemas","biotools"],"fetched_metadata":{"biotools":{"id":"scenery","home":"http://scenery.csd.uoc.gr","summary":"Apply standard pre-processing, statistical analysis, advanced visualization methods and network reconstruction methods on single-cell cytometry data. It has an open architecture that allows power users to extend its functionalities by submitting their own machine learning methods.","addition_date":"2017-06-29T11:53:45Z","last_update_date":"2020-06-16T10:55:21Z","tool_type":["Web service"],"version":["1.0"],"collections":["Proteomics"],"accessibility":"Open access","biotools_curie":"biotools:scenery","cost":"Free of charge","credit":[{"email":"geo.papoutsoglou@gmail.com","name":"Giorgos Papoutsoglou","typeEntity":"Person","typeRole":["Support"]},{"email":"jordan.xanthopoulos@gmail.com","name":"Iordanis Xanthopoulos","typeEntity":"Person","typeRole":["Maintainer"]},{"email":"geo.papoutsoglou@gmail.com","name":"Giorgos Papoutsoglou","typeEntity":"Person","typeRole":["Primary contact"],"url":"http://mensxmachina.org/en/people/giorgos-papoutsoglou/"},{"email":"tsamard.it@gmail.com","name":"Ioannis Tsamardinos","typeEntity":"Person","typeRole":["Primary contact"],"url":"http://mensxmachina.org/en/people/ioannis-tsamardinos/"},{"name":"European Research Council within the CausalPath project","typeEntity":"Funding agency","typeRole":["Contributor"]}],"documentation":[{"type":["General"],"url":"http://scenery.csd.uoc.gr/about.php"}],"edit_permission":{"authors":["proteomics.bio.tools"],"type":"group"},"function":[{"input":[{"data":{"term":"Matrix","uri":"http://edamontology.org/data_2082"},"format":[{"term":"Textual format","uri":"http://edamontology.org/format_2330"}]}],"note":"SCENERY accepts as input single-cell cytometry data in textual or .fcs format","operation":[{"term":"Pathway or network prediction","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_3439"},{"term":"Pathway or network visualisation","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_3083"},{"term":"Regression analysis","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_3659"},{"term":"Standardisation and normalisation","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_3435"},{"term":"Statistical inference","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_3658"},{"term":"Statistical modelling","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_3664"}],"output":[{"data":{"term":"Pathway or network","uri":"http://edamontology.org/data_2600"},"format":[{"term":"Biological pathway or network report format","uri":"http://edamontology.org/format_3166"},{"term":"Cytoscape input file format","uri":"http://edamontology.org/format_3477"},{"term":"HTML","uri":"http://edamontology.org/format_2331"},{"term":"svg","uri":"http://edamontology.org/format_3604"}]}]}],"maturity":"Mature","name":"SCENERY","operating_system":["Linux"],"owner":"gpap","publication":[{"doi":"10.1093/nar/gkx448","metadata":{"abstract":"\u00a9 2017 The Author(s).Flow and mass cytometry technologies can probe proteins as biological markers in thousands of individual cells simultaneously, providing unprecedented opportunities for reconstructing networks of protein interactions through machine learning algorithms. The network reconstruction (NR) problem has been well-studied by the machine learning community. However, the potentials of available methods remain largely unknown to the cytometry community, mainly due to their intrinsic complexity and the lack of comprehensive, powerful and easy-touse NR software implementations specific for cytometry data. To bridge this gap, we present Single CEll NEtwork Reconstruction sYstem (SCENERY), a web server featuring several standard and advanced cytometry data analysis methods coupled with NR algorithms in a user-friendly, on-line environment. In SCENERY, users may upload their data and set their own study design. The server offers several data analysis options categorized into three classes of methods: data (pre)processing, statistical analysis and NR. The server also provides interactive visualization and download of results as ready-to-publish images or multimedia reports. Its core is modular and based on the widely-used and robust R platform allowing power users to extend its functionalities by submitting their own NR methods.","authors":[{"name":"Athineou G."},{"name":"Elias S."},{"name":"Lagani V."},{"name":"Papoutsoglou G."},{"name":"Schmidt A."},{"name":"Tegnr J."},{"name":"Tsamardinos I."},{"name":"Xanthopoulos I."}],"citationCount":7,"date":"2017-07-03T00:00:00Z","journal":"Nucleic Acids Research","title":"SCENERY: A web application for (causal) network reconstruction from cytometry data"},"pmcid":"PMC5570263","pmid":"28525568","type":["Primary"]}],"topic":[{"term":"Computational biology","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_3307"},{"term":"Immunology","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_0804"},{"term":"Molecular interactions, pathways and networks","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_0602"},{"term":"Proteomics","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_0121"},{"term":"Statistics and probability","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_2269"}],"validated":1},"bioschemas":{"name":"SCENERY","home":"https://bio.tools/scenery","version":"1.0","summary":"Apply standard pre-processing, statistical analysis, advanced visualization methods and network reconstruction methods on single-cell cytometry data. It has an open architecture that allows power users to extend its functionalities by submitting their own machine learning methods.","tool_type":"sc:SoftwareApplication"},"oeb":{"metrics":[{"@id":"https://openebench.bsc.es/monitor/metrics/biotools:scenery:1.0/soap/scenery.csd.uoc.gr","@license":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/","@nmsp":"biotools","@type":"metrics","deprecated":true,"distribution":{"sourcecode":{"interpreted":false}},"project":{"build":{},"deployment":{},"documentation":{"general":true},"publications":[{"entries":[{"cit_count":7,"citations":[{"count":1,"year":"2020"},{"count":3,"year":"2019"},{"count":3,"year":"2021"}],"doi":"10.1093/nar/gkx448","pmcid":"PMC5570263","pmid":"28525568","ref_count":17,"refs":[{"count":1,"year":"2000"},{"count":1,"year":"2003"},{"count":1,"year":"2008"},{"count":1,"year":"2009"},{"count":1,"year":"2010"},{"count":1,"year":"2011"},{"count":2,"year":"2005"},{"count":2,"year":"2013"},{"count":2,"year":"2014"},{"count":2,"year":"2015"},{"count":3,"year":"2016"}],"title":"SCENERY: a web application for (causal) network reconstruction from cytometry data.","year":2017}]}],"summary":{"description":true},"website":{"bioschemas":false,"copyright":false,"https":false,"license":false,"operational":408,"redirects":[{"status":302,"url":"http://scenery.csd.uoc.gr/main.php"}],"ssl":null,"ssl_err":null}},"support":{"email":true}},{"@id":"https://openebench.bsc.es/monitor/metrics/scenery","@license":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/","@nmsp":null,"@type":"metrics","project":{"build":{},"deployment":{},"publications":[],"summary":{"description":true},"website":{"bioschemas":false,"copyright":false,"https":false,"license":false,"operational":408,"redirects":[{"status":302,"url":"http://scenery.csd.uoc.gr/main.php"}],"ssl":null,"ssl_err":null}}}]},"neubias":{"body":[{"format":"basic_html","processed":"<p>scenery is a scenegraphing and rendering library. It allows you to quickly create high-quality 3D visualisations based on mesh data. scenery contains both a OpenGL 4.1 and Vulkan renderer. The rendering pipelines of both renderers are configurable using YAML files, so it's easy to switch between e.g.&nbsp;<a href=\"https://github.com/scenerygraphics/scenery/blob/master/src/main/resources/graphics/scenery/backends/ForwardShading.yml\">Forward Shading</a>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<a href=\"https://github.com/scenerygraphics/scenery/blob/master/src/main/resources/graphics/scenery/backends/DeferredShading.yml\">Deferred Shading</a>, as well as&nbsp;<a href=\"https://github.com/scenerygraphics/scenery/blob/master/src/main/resources/graphics/scenery/backends/DeferredShadingStereo.yml\">stereo rendering</a>. Rendering pipelines can be switched on-the-fly.</p>\n\n<p>Both renderers support rendering to head-mounted VR goggles like the HTC Vive or Oculus Rift via&nbsp;<a href=\"https://github.com/ValveSoftware/openvr\">OpenVR/SteamVR</a>.</p>","summary":"","value":"<p>scenery is a scenegraphing and rendering library. It allows you to quickly create high-quality 3D visualisations based on mesh data. scenery contains both a OpenGL 4.1 and Vulkan renderer. The rendering pipelines of both renderers are configurable using YAML files, so it's easy to switch between e.g.&nbsp;<a href=\"https://github.com/scenerygraphics/scenery/blob/master/src/main/resources/graphics/scenery/backends/ForwardShading.yml\">Forward Shading</a>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<a href=\"https://github.com/scenerygraphics/scenery/blob/master/src/main/resources/graphics/scenery/backends/DeferredShading.yml\">Deferred Shading</a>, as well as&nbsp;<a href=\"https://github.com/scenerygraphics/scenery/blob/master/src/main/resources/graphics/scenery/backends/DeferredShadingStereo.yml\">stereo rendering</a>. Rendering pipelines can be switched on-the-fly.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Both renderers support rendering to head-mounted VR goggles like the HTC Vive or Oculus Rift via&nbsp;<a href=\"https://github.com/ValveSoftware/openvr\">OpenVR/SteamVR</a>.</p>\r\n"}],"changed":[{"format":"Y-m-d\\TH:i:sP","value":"2023-05-17T13:54:08+00:00"}],"created":[{"format":"Y-m-d\\TH:i:sP","value":"2018-01-28T11:33:53+00:00"}],"default_langcode":[{"value":true}],"attribution_instructions":[],"comments_2023":[{"cid":null,"comment_count":null,"last_comment_name":null,"last_comment_timestamp":null,"last_comment_uid":null,"status":2}],"free_tagging":[],"give_feedback_on_this_soft":[{"cid":0,"comment_count":0,"last_comment_name":null,"last_comment_timestamp":1517139511,"last_comment_uid":286,"status":2}],"has_author":[{"value":"G\u00fcnther Ulrik"}],"has_biological_terms":[],"has_comparison":[],"ha